Section name: RRR in MD
Excerpt:
In multi-dimensional cases (MD) where d>2, the contin- uous function space becomes problematic, the geometric shapes become complex, and even the operations such as computing the volume of a shape and the set operations be- come inefficient. Therefore, in this section, we use the k-set notion [ 17] to take an alternative route for solving the RRR problem by transforming the continuous function space to discrete sets. This leads to the design of an approximation algorithm that guarantees the rank-regret of k, introduces a log approximation-ratio in the output size, and runs in poly- nomial time, for a constant number of dimensions. We will explain the details of this algorithm in § 5.2. Then, in § 5.3, we propose the function-space partitioning algorithm mdrc that uses the result of Theorem 1 in its design for solving the problem without finding the k-sets. Note that proposed algorithms i

